cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its benchmark artifact, please cite it as below."
title: "Autopsy: detecting vulnerabilities in AI-generated code by reasoning across dependency graphs"
abstract: >-
  Autopsy is a static-plus-LLM vulnerability detector aimed at AI-generated code.
  It builds a cross-file dependency graph over Python, JavaScript, and
  TypeScript, scans code in overlapping line windows so that large files are not
  limited by a single pass's output budget, and enriches every finding with a
  graph-derived blast radius. Alongside the LLM pass it ships deterministic AST
  and graph detectors that need no model call: SQL strings interpolated into an
  execution sink, weak hashing of sensitive values, security gates whose return
  value is discarded, and deletion-based ("zero-footprint") vulnerabilities,
  where removing a comment boundary or a security control introduces a
  vulnerability that never appears as an added line in a diff. This repository is
  the reproducibility artifact accompanying the paper, including the benchmark
  harnesses, the Semgrep, Bandit, and CodeQL baselines scored by a frozen
  matcher, the pre-registered matched-budget control, and the August 2026
  replication with its qualitative failure analysis.
